    "body": "## Summary\r\n\r\nWhen a client uses SGLang’s typed Generate or TextGenerate gRPC RPC and does not provide an output-token limit, the API currently cannot distinguish between using the default limit (when max_new_tokens is absent) and having no caller-provided limit (when max_new_tokens is null). As a result, requests intended to generate up to the safe context and KV-cache limits are instead capped at the default of 128 tokens.\r\n\r\n## Changes\r\n\r\n- add `use_remaining_context` to the runtime gRPC sampling parameters\r\n- forward `max_new_tokens: null` when no explicit limit is provided and the option is enabled\r\n- preserve explicit `max_new_tokens` precedence and the existing default behavior\r\n\r\n## Testing\r\n\r\n- `cargo +1.93.1 fmt --all -- --check`\r\n- `cargo +1.93.1 test -p sglang-grpc`\r\n\r\n\r\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:white_check_mark: [Run #39186821477](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39186821477)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39186821453](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39186821453)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:heavy_minus_sign: **No AMD PR run found for this commit**.<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
